I am happy to announce Guppy 3 3.2.0

Guppy 3 is a library and programming environment for Python,
currently providing in particular the Heapy subsystem, which supports
object and heap memory sizing, profiling and debugging. It also
includes a prototypical specification language, the Guppy
Specification Language (GSL), which can be used to formally specify
aspects of Python programs and generate tests and documentation from a
common source.

Guppy 3 is a fork of Guppy-PE, created by Sverker Nilsson for Python 2.

This release adds support for Python 3.15, and support for Python 3.10
was dropped. Additionally, this release adds beta support for Free-Threaded
Python 3.14+, utilizing Stop-The-World for thread safety during heap traversal.

Other notable changes:

o All C extension modules types are now heap types.
o New wheels for Linux riscv64. [eshattow]
o NULL metatype encounters raise SystemError instead of segfaults. [emontnemery]
o Many iterables are now materialized into concrete tuples or immnodesets
  before iteration, due to thread-safety and stop-the-world-safety reasons.
o Reduced refcounting overhead during heap traversal.
o And many, many bug fixes...

